JDBC Adapter : (java data base connectivity)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Database communication.
Integration between SAP CPI and databases (SAP HANA, MySQL, SQL Server, Oracle, etc.)
Fetching master data (e.g., Product, Customer, Employee data)
Storing API logs or transactional data into a database
Triggering SQL queries from SAP applications

JDBC URL format :
jdbc:sqlserver://<virtualHost>:<virtualPort>;DatabaseName=<databaseName>;
Oracle uses jdbc:oracle:thin:@<host>[:<port>]:<SID>

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The JDBC adapter in SAP Cloud Platform Integration (CPI) enables integration flows to interact with database
systems, allowing for data exchange and manipulation. Key points include connecting to various databases
(cloud or on-premise), handling JDBC drivers and data sources, and supporting SQL operations and
stored procedures. It also facilitates error handling and recovery, including fallbacks to backup databases.